[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 7 (Android 2.3.7 Gingerbread) build for the [B]LG Optimus L3 E400[/B] (e0, Qualcomm MSM7x27A), built from a fresh device tree. The goal was to match the stock V10c behaviour wherever the stock is known to work: the kernel is the stock V10c zImage (with a single-instruction patch for the FM driver), and the graphics, camera and RIL blobs are the stock ones. Anything the ROM source does not cover is kept as small, reviewable patches in the device tree.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Early test build. Read the status list before flashing. Telephony is not verified yet.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status — Alpha[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]cm-7-20261028-UNOFFICIAL-e400.zip[/B]
Kernel: stock V10c with a one-instruction patch for the FM driver, Linux 2.6.38.6-perf #1 (Aug 8 2012)
Size: 84.5 MB
MD5: [B]a0010139016a84bd2ad4103dc5041e41[/B]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Basics:[/B] boot, reboot, power off, sleep and wake
[*][B]Display / GPU:[/B] Adreno 200 hardware rendering (no software fallback), auto-rotation without stripes
[*][B]Touch:[/B] multitouch, plus accelerometer, compass and proximity sensors
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, wired headset (also when plugged in before boot), microphone, voice recorder
[*][B]FM radio:[/B] works with the headset as antenna; it turns on and off without hanging (see known issues)
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect, browse
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] works, with a stable address across reboots
[*][B]Camera:[/B] photos up to 2048x1536 and hardware-encoded MPEG-4 video
[*][B]Storage:[/B] internal and external SD, USB mass storage
[*][B]Charging with the phone off:[/B] stock charger animation
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Partly done / untested[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]SIM / mobile network:[/B] the RIL is ported and the SIM reaches READY and LOADED with the IMSI read, but I could not register on a network yet. My own Movistar SIM was rejected by the network (probably a suspended SIM) and a SIM from another operator hits the carrier lock (the phone is an e0_mov_la, Movistar). [B]Calls, SMS and mobile data are NOT verified.[/B] I am getting another Movistar SIM to test.
[*][B]GPS:[/B] sees satellites, no fix yet
[*][B]Airplane mode, vibration[/B] and sensors beyond the basics: not tested
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]FM radio volume:[/B] the volume steps are still being tuned; the radio starts at a low level and the volume keys change it in coarse steps. The stock kernel's radio driver deadlocks when the radio reports an error, so the kernel in this zip has a one-instruction patch (tools/patch_kernel_fm.py in the device tree); the rest of the kernel is the stock V10c.
[/LIST]

